========================================================================================================
MODEL B — SMT DIVERGENCE  (vs BTC_USDT, read at the raid bar)
========================================================================================================
  4679 of 9175 signals (51%) show divergence: the symbol made a new 20-bar extreme and BTC_USDT did not.

                                                 R/sig      n       R/sig      n
  SMT  divergence  vs  none                     +0.037   4679  vs  -0.036   4496   diff +0.074  |z|  2.9  SEPARATES

  by direction — SMT's story is symmetric, so an effect on one
  side only is a directional bias, not SMT:
    longs                                       +0.042   2233  vs  -0.056   2143   diff +0.098  |z|  2.6  SEPARATES
    shorts                                      +0.033   2446  vs  -0.019   2353   diff +0.052  |z|  1.5

  THE CONTROL. confluence — the reference made the SAME extreme,
  so the sweep was real and nothing was trapped. SMT says this
  should be WORSE. if both beat the middle, the feature is reading
  'BTC_USDT did something' rather than the disagreement:
    confluence  vs  not                         -0.037   2722  vs  +0.017   6453   diff -0.054  |z|  1.9

    half 1                                      +0.038   2313  vs  -0.028   2290   diff +0.066  |z|  1.8
